  title: 'Formation of the Straits Settlements 1867 '
  info: "Singapore, along with Penang and Malacca, is reorganized under direct British
    administration as part of the Straits Settlements. This change strengthens the
    colony\u2019s governance and allows for more focused economic development. Infrastructure
    projects, such as the construction of roads, ports, and public buildings, accelerate.
    Singapore becomes a bustling entrep\xF4t for goods like tin, rubber, and spices,
    with its economy relying heavily on the labor of migrants.  "
